+# Local observation bridge correction
+
+After any OPS mutation, explicitly read the affected file with `ops_read_files` or the native read tool before native editing. A successful mutation is not a read: the bridge no longer registers the post-operation stat as observed. A previous observed version remains guarded and will become stale after the mutation. Dry runs, partial results, failures and interrupted results also do not refresh observations.
+
+The normal successful explicit read/stat bridge remains unchanged. It snapshots the host version before starting the worker, so a concurrent change cannot be endorsed using a newer post-read stat. It relies on the host provider's version/freshness contract; it is not a new content-hash or atomic read guarantee.
+
+The worker's published content digest cannot be equated with a provider's opaque metadata version. Removing post-mutation refresh is the conservative JS-only correction; no Rust worker or host API changes are required. Native edits still require the observation-policy plugin and provider guard.
